      "content": "The principle of self-ownership strongly supports the free speech argument by asserting that the individual has absolute control over their own mind and body, which logically must include their ideas and digital voice. If one is the ultimate owner of the self, then the state, an external political entity, has no moral right to dictate the content of that self's discourse. Therefore, government regulation is seen as an unjust incursion into the most fundamental right of the self to determine one's own thoughts and expression.",
